ple pairs (W4, B6, B7) for flexibility.\n\nReason: Playing B5 optimizes my hand structure by maintaining three clear chow potentials (W2-W3-W4, T3-T4-T5, B6-B7-B8) while keeping multiple pairs (W4-W4, B6-B6, B7-B7) for maximum flexibility. This gives me the best chance to form a winning hand with at least 8 points through patterns like \"All Chows\" + \"All Simples\" + potential waiting patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play B5"}
